.TITLE "pwd"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Prints the full absolute path of the current working directory. It helps users __orient__ themselves within the filesystem.

.DIV "TLDR"
**pwd**
Displays the full path of the directory you are currently in.
> 

**pwd -P**
Displays the physical directory path, resolving any symbolic links.
> __-P__ physical flag

.DIV "SUMMARY"
While __pwd__ usually shows the logical path, using __pwd -P__ is essential when you need to know the actual location of a symlinked directory on the disk.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**linux:cd** **linux:ls** **linux:stat**

